(text "LATCHING VALVE DRIVER (MX1508 - the chip on the \"mini L298N\" module)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 208 0) (effects (font (size 2 2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f63867dc-df82-4b11-b9f0-b249fa26261e"))
(text "U403 = MX1508, channel 1: IN1 (GPIO27) high = OUTA high (open); IN2 (GPIO5) high = OUTB high (close); both low = standby\n< 0.1 uA. Same logic as the module, so the firmware does not change. Its motor supply must stay below 10 V, so the 12 V boost\ncharges C403 through a 78L09 (current-limited, ~0.1 A) and D403 to ~8.7 V; C403 then supplies the coil pulse, and D403 keeps it\ncharged while the boost is off. JP401 (solder jumper): 1-2 = 8.7 V reservoir (9 V valves, default), 2-3 = cell (3.6-6 V valves).\nFirmware: SENS_EN on >= 1 s before a pulse (tops up C403). Logic supply = +3V3, so the 3.3 V inputs are always in range." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20 212 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4f95b37a-3186-42da-ab0e-2818592462f3"))
